BanMido wrote:
>
> I am yet to find a silver saber, I am not sure where I can get
> one unless a weapon shop is generated somewhere with it.

Early on the watch captain in mine town has a 50-50 chance of carrying a
long sword (good for conversion to Excalibur) or a silver saber.  It's
worth trying to keep your original pet alive until it can take out the
watch captain on the way back up from mines end.  It's a trade off in
giving pets enough monsters to gain experience in the early game - I've
lost a fair number of pets my first time in mine town because they got
mean enough to attack the watch captain and then died from long sword
damage.  Pets attack based on the strength of the unarmed monster.

Deeper I think it's randomly generated captains who have the same 50-50
chance in armament.  Go deep enough long enough and you'll encounter
enough captains eventually to become pretty sure to get a silver saber.

I don't recall using a Castle wand wish on a silver saber but I might
have done so years ago and forgotten.  I've wished for a blessed +3
rustproof athame that I can remember.  Having that initial katana gives
you a good enough off hand weapon it's worth fighting hostile captains
but not worth a wish.


